  "id": "DrugBank_DB00046 - MONDO_5015",
  "verbalization": "Insulin Lispro, a long-acting insulin analog, is linked to Diabetes Mellitus (disease) through a series of indirect pathways. The evidence suggests that Insulin Lispro is indicated for Type 2 Diabetes Mellitus, and this indication is supported by its relationship with Voglibose, a drug used to treat Diabetes Mellitus. Additionally, Insulin Lispro is also associated with Diabetic Ketoacidosis, which is linked to Insulin Glulisine, another insulin analog that is indicated for Diabetes Mellitus. These pathways highlight a potential mechanism by which Insulin Lispro may influence the development or management of diabetes, though the exact mechanism remains unclear. The integration of these relationships underscores the complex interplay between insulin analogs and diabetes, emphasizing the role of indirect pathways in drug-repurposing efforts.",
